  "title": "Dwight M NDE 6265",
  "date": "July 1964",
  "content": "Next I awoke. Another lifeguard, Jeff, had come out to watch. After I stopped moving in the water, he quickly came out got me and applied backpressure arm lift resuscitation and I came to. I was in a tunnel. Everything outside the tunnel was moving very fast. At the time, it seemed to be like looking outside a train window. Melvin Morse, MD has or had two websites; one opens showing a small figure inside a tunnel and my tunnel looked exactly like that. Nothing else I have found accurately describes the tunnel. Afterward I was both exited and disappointed. I knew there was a lot more I didn't experience NDERF note: we believe that he is describing the painting 'Ascent of the Blessed' by Hieronymus Bosch",
